       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline, which is 200 mg/day for adults. Doses above that haven't been shown to work better, and they raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and agitation. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nPlease check whether one of these applies:\n\n- **Typo or unit error.** Did you mean 40 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg?\n- **Intended dose.** If you want the maximum, I can enter 200 mg by mouth once daily. Usual practice is to start at 25\u201350 mg and titrate up by 25\u201350 mg at weekly intervals or longer.\n- **Deliberate supra-maximal dosing.** If this is intentional, for example on a psychiatry recommendation, tell me and add the rationale. I can enter it with a note, but pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter the order."
      }
